    "body": "Based on #36356 and #36921. **Only the last commit is new.**\n\nAfter a mempool change, `getblocktemplate` only rebuilds its cached template once it's more than 5 seconds old, and it measures that age with the system clock. That works fine in practice, but as pointed out in a [review comment](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36356#discussion_r4562199844), a steady clock is the better fit for measuring an interval, since system time changes don't affect it.\n\nThis switches to the steady clock, like #30372 did for `RandAddSeedPerfmon`. Since `setmocktime` doesn't move it, `mining_prioritisetransaction.py` now waits out the 5 seconds, and the unit test uses a fake steady clock.",
