      "message": "rpc: gather the getblocktemplate cache state into a struct\n\nReplace the function-local statics in getblocktemplate with a\nCachedBlockTemplate struct and a GetNewOrCachedBlockTemplate() helper,\nboth local to rpc/mining.cpp. The cache is still process-wide, but it is\nnow GUARDED_BY(::cs_main), so its synchronization is checked.\n\nGetNewOrCachedBlockTemplate() keeps the existing rules: the template is\nrebuilt when the tip changes, or when the mempool changed and the cached\ntemplate is more than 5 seconds old. A failed rebuild leaves the cached\ntemplate unset so that the next call tries again.\n\nThis prepares for moving the cache into BlockTemplateManager in the next\ncommit. While the code is still next to the original, it also:\n\n- Drops the static CBlockIndex pointer. pindexPrev is looked up from the\n  template's hashPrevBlock, so it cannot outlive the ChainstateManager\n  that owns it.\n- Reads the active chain tip inside GetNewOrCachedBlockTemplate() and\n  compares it with the template's hashPrevBlock, so the cache cannot\n  pair a template with a tip it does not build on. The caller no longer\n  needs to re-read the tip after longpolling.\n- Builds the longpollid from hashPrevBlock, so it always names the block\n  the template builds on.\n- Replaces the deprecated GetTime() with the equivalent\n  Now<NodeSeconds>().\n- Names the 5 second rebuild interval GBT_TEMPLATE_REBUILD_INTERVAL.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "w0xlt",
        "email": "94266259+w0xlt@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T00:09:14Z"
      },
